MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_001: *cough* *cough*
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_002: Ah, the Promised One. Did you require something?
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_003: Did you happen to hear my fit of coughing? I am\nsorry you witnessed that. But you need not worry.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_004: Hrk! *cough* *cough*
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_005: Ah!
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_006: It is nothing serious. Age catches up with us all.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_007: I am on the wrong side of 50—perhaps a little bit too\nold to still be on the front lines.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_008: Many years past the first polite inquiries I received\nabout my retirement.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_009: I always told them I would rather remain on the\nbattlefield until my strength failed me.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_010: Now here I am, still fighting at my advanced age.\nI may be getting my wish.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_011: In truth, I sometimes envy those who bear the\nbloodline of gods.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_012: If I had their longevity, I could fight on and pass\ndown all I have learned to future generations.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_013: <NCA>"Even gods perish eventually."
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_014: Ah. I cannot argue the point.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_015: Fortunate for us, as we are attempting to kill one.\nIt was an idle thought, nothing more.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_016: I've never voiced it before because I deemed it\ndisrespectful to the true gods, such as Yu Phas.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_017: Strangely, I have no such concerns when it comes\nto you, Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_018: Perhaps because you are the Herald whose arrival in\nthis land was foretold long ago.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_019: <NCA>"You can come to me with anything."
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_020: <NCB>"I'm not as impressive as you may think."
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_021: <ACA>Haha. One would never know you are the\nPromised One from your gentle manner.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_022: <ACB>You are an odd one. The people laud you as their\nPromised One, yet you profess to be just like them.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_023: That said, please find it in your generous heart to\noverlook an old man's stubbornness awhile more.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_024: I suspect I will see no wars after this one. But until\nBalor is overthrown, I shall fight on.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_025: Ah!
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_026: Thank you for indulging me.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_027: But the Mastermind of Saramis is still the equal of\nany on the battlefield, even now.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_A_028: Be certain that I shall prove my worth in whatever\ncapacity you see fit.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_001: Ah! Is that you, Promised One?
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_002: It gladdens my heart to see you alive!
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_003: But how did you escape the underworld's collapse?\nPardon—we need not speak of it. It matters not.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_004: It is an honor to behold you again.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_005: <NCA>"Is now the time for such formality?"
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_006: Hoho. I see the end of the war has done nothing to\nchange you.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_007: But as you are a hero to all the world, I must afford\nyou the proper respect.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_008: As for me...with no foe left to vanquish, I find myself\nwithout a role to play.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_009: As the youth find their places upon the stage, their\nelders must exit.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_010: I shall be a stagehand now—working to support my\npeople from behind the scenes.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_011: Until the day the curtain falls.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_012: Mm...
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_013: There is no cause for dismay. I can think of no finer\nway to live out my remaining years.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_014: I've always devoted myself fully to the kingdom.\nAnd I do not regret that choice.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_015: With Balor defeated and Saramis free from the yoke\nof Dagda, my kingdom will prosper ever more.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_016: I only hope that my name will be some small footnote\nwhen the histories are written.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_017: Compared to the majesty of Queen Theodora, I fear\nthat one such as I might slip into obscurity.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_018: <NCA>"I'll remember you."
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_019: <NCB>"I'll make sure your legend lives on."
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_020: <ACA>I am grateful that you should say so, Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_021: <ACB>You will? That is more than I could dare dream,\nPromised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_022: <NCA>"But only if you loosen up."
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_023: That is not such a simple request. As I said, you are\na hero to all the world.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_024: Though, seen another way, a hero's request ought\nto be granted.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_025: <RSDS>Very well. Though it pains me, I shall endeavor to\ndo as you ask.
MID_SE_Ism_Bon_S_026: I have enough time to make the attempt. I hope that\nyou will spend that time with me.